# Confidence Engine Rules

## Explicit Scores

Every promoted finding must carry:

- `confidence_score` in `[0,1]` or enumerated buckets with numeric mapping.
- `evidence_strength` breakdown (static proof depth, test outcomes, graph path specificity).
- `known_fp_family` tags when applicable.

## Features Only

Scores derive from **observable features**: graph path quality, sanitizer coverage, hook context certainty, duplicate historical FP rate, verification results — not LLM self-assessment alone.

## Calibration

- Maintain evaluation sets with labeled outcomes; track precision/recall per bucket; recalibrate when schema/rules change materially.

## Thresholds

- Define promotion thresholds for internal vs external reporting; sub-threshold items remain “candidates.”

## Transparency

- Document limitations (dynamic calls unresolved, partial repo context) as explicit score penalties.

## Anti-Patterns

- “Model certainty” without cross-checks is invalid for High/Critical externally visible outputs.
